2．Experimental Methods
2.1Preparationbeforeexperiment
(1) Preheated two water baths to 37℃ and 85℃;
(2) Prepared SIF and E-SIF, incubate in advance in the water bath. Pancreatin
(Maclin, cat#P916050) contains a variety of enzymes, including protease,
amylase, lipase, etc.
2.2Reactiontubes
(1) Labeled three 2mlcentrifuge tubes as Pmix,Emix, Dmix;
(2) Labeled thirteen 1.5mL tubes as P1/10, P0, P120, D0, D2, D5, D10, D20, D30,
D60, D120, E0, E120,and added 10μl PLB to each tube.
2.3ProteinSolution
(1) Ptube:Thawed theprotein extract sample toroom temperature, pipettean
appropriateamount ofsolution and marked as Ptube(13.25mg/ml);
