(2) Pdtube: Pipetted a portionof thesolutionfrom the Ptube, diluted the
concentration to 1/10, and marked as Pd (10μLP+90μLwater);
(3) RUBISCOsolution:Prepared a2mg/ml RUBISCO solution.
2.4Preparationof digestion, protein, andenzyme controls.

(1) Protein solution, pancreatin solution, and water were preheated separately for 5
minutesin 37℃ before thestart of each experiment;
(2) P1/10:Added 38μLE-SIF,quickly heated to 85℃for 5minutes, pipette 10μLof
protein solution from the Pd tube, mixed well, heated at 85℃ for 5 minutes, and
stored onice;
(3) D0:Added 38 μL E-SIF into two 1.5mL centrifuge tubes, quickly heated to 85℃
for 10 minutes, pipetted 10 μL of protein solution from the P tube or RUBISCO
solution,mixed well, heated at 85℃ for5minutes, and stored onice;
(4) Pmx (protein control without pancreatin): Pipetted 50μL from the P tube or
RUBISCOsolution,added 190μLSIF and mixed well;
P0: Pipetted 40μL from Pmx, mixed well, heated at 85℃ for 5 minutes, and
stored onice;
P120: Heated the remaining Pmx at 37℃ for 120 minutes, pipetted 40μL into
P120,mixed well, heated at 85℃for 5minutes, and stored onice;
(5) Emx (pancreatin control without protein): Pipetted 50μL of water, added 190μL
E-SIF and mixed well;
E0: Pipetted 40μL from Emx, mixed well, heated at 85℃ for 5 minutes, and
stored onice;
E120: Heated the remaining Emx at 37℃ for 120 minutes, pipetted 40μL into
E120, mixed well, heated at 85℃for 5minutes, and stored onice;
(6) Dmx (digestion mixture): Pipetted 100μLfrom the Ptube or RUBISCO solution,
added 380μL E-SGF into two micro centrifuge tubes and mixed well, placed
Dmx in 37℃ water bath, pipetted 40μL of the digestion mixture at 2, 5, 10, 20,
30, 60,120 minutes into D2-D120 tubes respectively, immediately heated each
tubeto 85℃for 5minutes,and stored onice.
